  "version": "ksic-ff12-v1",
  "title": "KSIC to Fama-French 12 industries (ratings-v1, Korea)",
  "method": "Each KSIC division (2 digits) maps to the FF12 industry that Ken French's Siccodes12 definition gives the closest US SIC analog ('sic'). Longer codes in 'overrides' (3-5 digits) take precedence over their division; the longest matching prefix of a company's OpenDART induty_code wins. A code whose division is absent is unmapped: unless it is a financial code, the member stays eligible with issue universe_fetch_error (fetchError 'unmapped_ksic') and is scored insufficient; only the financial rules exclude.",
  "sources": {
    "ksic": "Statistics Korea, Korean Standard Industrial Classification, 10th revision (2017); division numbering unchanged in the 11th revision. Company codes from OpenDART company.json induty_code.",
    "ff12": "https://mba.tuck.dartmouth.edu/pages/faculty/ken.french/ftp/Siccodes12.zip"
  },
  "financialExclusion": "docs/ratings-v1.md section 2 excludes KSIC 64, 65, 66 and 68 but keeps 64992 (holding companies). Only those excluded codes map to Money, so eligible members never carry Money. OpenDART also codes financial holding companies 64992 (KB금융 and 신한지주 verified 2026-10-06); ratings/sectors.py excludes a 64992 issuer whose registered name contains 금융지주 (reason 'financial_holding').",
